# caller-owned quic and http/3 socket runtime
#
# failure scope. a datagram that cannot be handled costs that datagram, and a
# connection that cannot be served costs that connection: it is failed, and its
# release is retried on later passes until everything it holds is returned.
# neither ever fails the runtime, because the runtime failing releases every
# pump and with it every other connection. `advance` returns FAILED only when a
# pump can no longer receive, since a pump that stops reading is an outage
# nothing on a later pass would repair. `snapshot` counts the scoped failures.

